    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**14 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core feature set works well: dashboard creation and editing, venue/vendor filtering and search (case-insensitive, across names, descriptions, locations, and specialties), favorites, checklist browsing by category, task completion with progress rollup, and localStorage persistence across navigation and reload.\n\n**Five defects found — four are clustered in input validation:**\n\n1. **CS-8 — Budget validation missing.** Saving `0` or `-500` succeeded silently; dashboard rendered `$0` and `$-500`, overwriting the valid saved budget.\n2. **CS-9 — Guest count validation missing.** `-20` and `85.5` were both accepted and displayed verbatim.\n3. **CS-11 — Wedding date validation missing.** A past date (2020-03-15) was accepted, and as a side effect the countdown element vanished from the hero entirely.\n4. **IX-19 — Cancel doesn't discard the draft.** The dashboard correctly kept its saved values, so this is easy to miss, but the editor's form state is never reset — reopening it showed `DISCARD ME` / `999999` / `7`. A user who cancels and reopens sees stale edits and could save them believing they're the stored values.\n5. **IX-12 — Detail views entirely non-functional.** \"View Details\" (venues) and \"View Profile\" (vendors) are inert: no modal, no route change, no console error. There is no path to a listing's full details anywhere in the app.\n\nTwo notes worth flagging beyond the raw verdicts. The validation failures (CS-8/9/11) share one root cause — the save handler commits raw field values with no guard — so a single fix in the wedding-details save path would likely close all three. And IX-12 is the most user-visible gap, since the buttons render as normal affordances while doing nothing at all."
  }
}
